/* Learning Data: Governance you can use, in English: the words of the series' labs (training) and scenarios (evaluation), for all
   six films. Keep the keys in step with learn.es.js. assets/governance-in-practice/learn.js draws them; "vis" names a picture in
   its PIX, which takes its words from the lab (w) or the scenario (st).
   site-tools/build_series.py reads this file as text (series_learn): "labs:[" and "qs:[" each start a line; each lab's first keys
   are id, kind, film, chapter (a chapter id of its film, or null until the film is made), c and name, in that order, its id made of
   letters, digits and _ only; each scenario's are type, n (its film's number times ten, plus its place), lab and film. No other
   object here starts with an id, and no other key is called kind or starts an object with type (they're counted).
   Names, numbers and dates follow each film's script and narration: check a film's labs and scenarios against them when it changes.
   close: the series' last words, under the scenarios' results for all films and for the last film: that film's closing chapter
   (chapter), in its own words, and in learn.es.js in its Spanish captions. */
